# Keep the cross-platform launchers byte-identical on every checkout.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is common on Windows and rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout. For rpa.sh that breaks the `#!/usr/bin/env sh` interpreter line
# (and every embedded command) as soon as the skill is copied into a POSIX
# environment, so it must stay LF regardless of the local autocrlf setting.
# rpa.cmd is pinned to LF as well so both launchers behave the same way and
# the tree does not drift between platforms.
#
# Scope is deliberately limited to these two paths: the rest of the repository
# predates this file and is checked out as CRLF on Windows, so adding blanket
# `text` attributes elsewhere would produce a large renormalisation diff.

*.sh  text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=lf
